-granting-judgment-to-the-officials-on-count-ii-because--115646-rsmo-passes-strict-scrutiny-in-that-it-advances-missouris-compelling-interest-in-ensuring-that-elections-are-fair-and-appear-fair-and-in-avoiding-first-amendment-issues-that-would-arise-by-compelling-taxpayers-to-pay-for-speech-with-which-they-disagree-and-the-law-is-narrowly-tailored-to-achieve-those-interests-1)1026 0 R(ii-the-circuit-courts-decision)1017 0 R(iii-the-circuit-court-erred-in-granting-judgment-to-the-officials-on-count-iii-because--115646-is-not-unconstitutionally-vague-in-that-vagueness-does-not-permeate-the-statute-as-is-necessary-to-succeed-on-a-facial-vagueness-challenge-since-there-is-a-core-of-conduct-to-which-the-statute-clearly-applies)1022 0 R(iii-the-circuit-court-erred-in-granting-judgment-to-the-officials-on-count-iii-because--115646-is-not-unconstitutionally-vague-in-that-vagueness-does-not-permeate-the-statute-as-is-necessary-to-succeed-on-a-facial-vagueness-challenge-since-there-is-a-core-of-conduct-to-which-the-statute-clearly-applies-1)1029 0 R(iii-the-general-assembly-amends--115646-rsmo)1018 0 R(introduction)1014 0 R(jurisdictional-statement)1013 0 R(points-relied-on)1019 0 R(statement-of-facts)1015 0 R]>>>>>>
